WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.492
Freshness policy is part of the data product.

00:00:03.492 --> 00:00:08.712
Consumers need to know how often the materialized view refreshes.

00:00:08.712 --> 00:00:12.492
They need a way to see the last successful refresh.

00:00:12.492 --> 00:00:16.242
The team should know what happens when refresh fails.

00:00:16.242 --> 00:00:21.802
And the expected maximum latency should be documented rather than assumed.

00:00:21.802 --> 00:00:27.702
A standard view stores a query definition, not a separate copy of the rows.

00:00:27.702 --> 00:00:35.367
Treat the selected columns, names, types, and grain as a contract with downstream users.

00:00:35.367 --> 00:00:42.240
Changing that contract can break dashboards or applications even if the underlying query still runs.
